<title>SLOVAKIA: Details of Slovak May 1997 consumer inflation.</title>
<headline>Details of Slovak May 1997 consumer inflation.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are details of Slovak consumer inflation for May as released by the Statistical Bureau (SUSR) on Tuesday.</p>
<p> SLOVAK CONSUMER INFLATION	May 97    April 97   May 96</p>
<p>  pct change mo/mo		   0.1	  0.5	 0.5</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr		   6.1	  6.3	 n/a(1.9)</p>
<p>Foodstuffs, soft drinks</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	  -0.9	  0.7	 0.3</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     6.2	  7.5	 n/a(0.5)</p>
<p>Alcohol and tobacco products</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.2	  0.2	 0.1</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     3.8	  4.0	 n/a(1.8)</p>
<p>Clothes and shoes</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   1.0	  0.6	 0.9</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     7.7	  7.6	 n/a(2.7)</p>
<p>Household, energy, utilities and fuels</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.2	  0.4	 0.1</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     6.8	  5.1	 n/a(1.5)</p>
<p>Furniture, household appliances and maintenance</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.3	  0.7	 0.4</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     4.6	  4.8	 n/a(1.5)</p>
<p>Healthcare</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   4.1	  0.9	 0.7</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    13.3	  7.2	 n/a(4.8)</p>
<p>Transportation</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.4	  0.2	 1.9</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     5.4	  6.9	 n/a(2.5)</p>
<p>Leisure and culture</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.0	  0.7	-0.3</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     4.6	  4.2	 n/a(7.1)</p>
<p>Education</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.7	  0.1	 2.6</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     9.2	 11.2	 n/a(-0.9)</p>
<p>Hotels, cafes, restaurants</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.4	  0.4	 0.6</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     6.6	  7.1	 n/a(1.2)</p>
<p>Various goods and services</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.5	  0.3	 0.3</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     5.1	  4.7	 n/a(0.9)</p>
<p>Note. SUSR said that due to the changes in the population's expenditure structure, it had revised formulas for calcuating CPI, using 1995 as a base year.</p>
<p>SUSR released revised month-on-month figures for 1996 under the new methodology, but it did not release revised year-on-year figures for 1996. Figures in parentheses show changes against December 1995, the base month for the new formula.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521-8402</p>
